From: Pat Wendorf <dungeons@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] battery: no battery icon on machines without a system battery

The upower subscription (cosmic-settings ae5c750, pinned by epoch-1.8)
reports NoBattery once and then keeps forwarding UPower changes as
Update events. On a desktop with a wireless mouse or keyboard (a UPower
"battery" that is not a power supply) the first change flipped the
applet to a 0% battery icon. cosmic-settings a366fc7 (epoch-1.9) ends
the stream instead; do the equivalent here: after NoBattery, ignore
Update events.

Upstream: fixed in cosmic-settings a366fc7 (epoch-1.9)
---
diff --git a/cosmic-applet-battery/src/app.rs b/cosmic-applet-battery/src/app.rs
index f5113eff..0c425744 100644
--- a/cosmic-applet-battery/src/app.rs
+++ b/cosmic-applet-battery/src/app.rs
@@ -79,6 +79,9 @@ struct CosmicBatteryApplet {
     charging_limit: Option<bool>,
     battery_percent: f64,
     no_battery: bool,
+    // UPower reported no system battery (a battery that powers the machine,
+    // not a wireless mouse or keyboard); stays set, see UpowerDevice below.
+    no_system_battery: bool,
     on_battery: bool,
     gpus: FxHashMap<PathBuf, GPUData>,
     update_trigger: Option<UnboundedSender<()>>,
@@ -404,6 +407,11 @@ impl cosmic::Application for CosmicBatteryApplet {
                 }
             }
             Message::UpowerDevice(event) => match event {
+                // The subscription reports NoBattery once, then keeps passing
+                // on UPower changes (fixed upstream in cosmic-settings a366fc7,
+                // after epoch-1.8): a peripheral's charge level then showed a
+                // 0% battery on a desktop. No system battery means no updates.
+                DeviceDbusEvent::Update { .. } if self.no_system_battery => {}
                 DeviceDbusEvent::Update {
                     on_battery,
                     percent,
@@ -415,6 +423,7 @@ impl cosmic::Application for CosmicBatteryApplet {
                 }
                 DeviceDbusEvent::NoBattery => {
                     self.no_battery = true;
+                    self.no_system_battery = true;
                 }
             },
             Message::KeyboardBacklight(event) => match event {
